course: dictionary
lesson: 3792
title: Footwork
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Footwork is the way you move your feet. Footballers, boxers, tennis players and dancers all need good footwork, and coaches train it in PE. In «fast, strong footwork», the words fast and strong tell you it is a kind of movement, not something you wear.
explain: Use the swap test. Put in "moving your feet" instead of footwork and check the sentence still makes sense. Context clues show you which meaning the author means.
explain: Footwork can also be an informal phrase. «Some fancy footwork» means clever, quick actions that get you out of a difficult situation. If the words nearby are about trouble or tricky questions, this is the meaning to choose.
fact: Footwork means the way a person moves their feet.
fact: In sport and dancing, coaches train footwork so players can dodge, turn and keep their balance.
fact: «Good footwork» means skilful, controlled movement of the feet.
fact: Informal: «fancy footwork» means clever, quick actions to escape a difficult situation.
fact: Footwork is an uncountable noun, so we say «good footwork», not «a good footworks».
exercise: Quick footwork helped her dodge the ball. What does footwork mean here? | A pair of new trainers | *The way she moved her feet | The ball she threw to her friend | The rules of the game
exercise: Flamenco dancers use «fast, strong footwork». What is the footwork? | A sad feeling in the heart | *Fast, strong moves of the feet | Loud singing with clapping hands | A guitar played slowly
exercise: The coach says, «Work on your footwork before the match.» What should the player practise? | Shouting at the referee | *Moving their feet well | Eating a healthy breakfast | Stretching their neck
test: «He used some fancy footwork to avoid answering the tricky question.» What does fancy footwork mean here? | Losing his shoes in the mud | Dancing very fast on the stage | *Clever moves to get out of a difficult situation | Asking his teacher for help
test: When her brain's alarm fires, «fine footwork get worse», so what happens to her footwork? | It gets better | It is no longer needed | *It gets worse | It turns into a dance
exam: Hannah says footwork is a type of shoe. Why is she wrong? | Footwork means a kind of sports ball | Footwork is a shoe worn only by dancers | *Footwork means the way you move your feet, not a shoe | Footwork is a team that plays football
